  "scope": "Three pad.19 records use a stronger global maximum-width bound. Each complete connected drawn-plus-native-fill metal component must fit in a strip no wider than 25 um for met1/met2 or 6 um for met3, measured as the shorter side of its axis-aligned bounding box. A subset selected beneath a pad cannot have greater local thickness than its containing strip. No pad selector, clipping boundary or local feature exemption is needed for a passing bound. Drawing and fill are unioned across the full reachable hierarchy before measuring; touching fragments cannot be checked separately. Explicit mask/edit and alternate metal-purpose data prevent promotion because their effect on the final conductor is not established here. At the exact maximum the bound passes. A larger box, including a thin L or ring, remains unreviewed rather than being called a pad-rule violation. Other under-pad spacing, minimum width, pad construction and generated-mask requirements remain separate.",
